###
# LikesController requests
#
# Run the login request first. REST Client stores the response and uses the
# token variable below for the authenticated requests.

@baseUrl = https://localhost:5001/api
@targetMemberId = todd-id
@token = {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Login as a seeded user (Lisa)
# Seeded users use the password: Pa$$w0rd
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "lisa@test.com",
  "password": "Pa$$w0rd"
}

### Get the IDs of members Lisa currently likes
GET {{baseUrl}}/likes/list
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Like Todd (running this request again toggles the like off)
POST {{baseUrl}}/likes/{{targetMemberId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get members Lisa likes
GET {{baseUrl}}/likes?predicate=liked
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get members who like Lisa
GET {{baseUrl}}/likes?predicate=likedBy
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get mutual likes (matches)
GET {{baseUrl}}/likes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Toggle Todd's like off again (optional cleanup)
# POST {{baseUrl}}/likes/{{targetMemberId}}
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### This should return 401 because no token is supplied
GET {{baseUrl}}/likes/list
